{"id":"406deba91f42e16246259a90e94a9b410c626b30","axis":"silent","repo":"dotnet/roslyn","sha":"406deba91f42e16246259a90e94a9b410c626b30","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".github/instructions/Razor.instructions.md","lines":["@@ -65,9 +65,9 @@ their original sub-tree layout","   embedded quotes are escaped without changing their values."," - **Remote services**: Place the public stub method (calling `RunServiceAsync`) directly","   above its private implementation method.","-- **Formatting options across OOP**: Cohost endpoints must resolve","-  `CSharpSyntaxFormattingOptions` from the Razor document's analyzer-config options with","-  `razorDocument.GetCSharpSyntaxFormattingOptions(cancellationToken)`.","+- **Formatting options across OOP**: Cohost endpoints use","+  `razorDocument.GetRazorFormattingOptions(clientSettings, cancellationToken)` to resolve","+  Razor preferences and `CSharpSyntaxFormattingOptions` from the Razor document's analyzer-config options.","   This applies `.editorconfig` sections matching the `.razor` or `.cshtml` path and falls back to","   the user's global C# options. Include the resolved options in `RazorFormattingOptions` sent to","   remote formatting consumers; remote `IClientSettingsManager` state does not contain the user's"],"additions":3,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":".github/memory/testing/razor.md","lines":["@@ -24,6 +24,12 @@ Layer-specific test guidance for Razor tooling/compiler tests under `src/Razor`.","   paths and contents through `additionalFiles`. `CohostTestBase` registers files","   named `.editorconfig` as analyzer-config documents, including nested configs,","   so endpoints resolve options through the production path.","+- Shared cohost tests run on Windows and Unix. Use `CohostTestBase.FilePath` for","+  document and analyzer-config paths (and `Path.Combine` for nested segments),","+  rather than hard-coded Windows paths. On Unix, backslashes are filename","+  characters, so `Path.GetFileName` will not recognise `C:\\path\\to\\.editorconfig`","+  as an analyzer config. Keep configs and documents under the same project root","+  so the config applies to the document."," - Integration tests using `AdditionalSyntaxTrees` for tag helper discovery must","   set `UseTwoPhaseCompilation => true` (see `ComponentDiscoveryIntegrationTest`).","   Under two-phase compilation the `AdditionalSyntaxTrees` are compiled into a"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/razor/Formatting.md","lines":["@@ -25,10 +25,9 @@ Check that log first when formatting seems to be a no-op."," ## The formatter changes code in ways I don't want"," "," Razor's formatter delegates HTML formatting to your IDE's HTML formatter and C# formatting to","-Roslyn. That means Razor can produce results you don't expect or that don't match your","-language-specific settings. For example, we do not currently support `.editorconfig` (see","-[dotnet/razor#4406](https://github.com/dotnet/razor/issues/4406)), so settings there may not","-affect Razor formatting.","+Roslyn. C# formatting options are read from `.editorconfig` sections matching the `.razor`","+or `.cshtml` file, not the generated C# file. HTML formatting still depends on your IDE's","+HTML formatter settings."," "," If the formatter changes your code incorrectly, open an issue and include:"," ","@@ -42,6 +41,27 @@ repro if you can — smaller repros help us diagnose and fix the issue faster."," Also enable formatting logging and attach the logs to the issue; those logs contain useful"," diagnostic information we need to investigate formatting bugs."," ","+## Configure Razor formatting with editorconfig","+","+The IDE and `dotnet format` read these Razor-specific options from `.editorconfig`:","+","+```editorconfig","+[*.{razor,cshtml}]","+razor_code_block_brace_on_next_line = false","+# Valid attribute indent styles: align_with_first, indent_by_one, indent_by_two","+razor_attribute_indent_style = align_with_first","+razor_ignore_indentation_in_script_or_style_blocks_with_complex_razor = true","+```","+","+These are the default values. `razor_attribute_indent_style` also accepts `indent_by_one`","+and `indent_by_two`, which indent continuation attributes by one or two levels relative","+to the tag instead of aligning them with its first attribute. The other options accept","+`true` or `false`.","+","+Valid values override your IDE preferences for the matching files. Missing or invalid","+values leave the IDE preference unchanged; `dotnet format` uses the defaults above.","+Editor triggers such as format-on-type and format-on-paste remain IDE settings.","+"," ## Turn on Formatting Logging"," "," 1. Create a folder on your machine to receive logs."],"additions":24,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Razor/src/Razor/src/Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.Razor.CohostingShared/CodeActions/CohostCodeActionsResolveEndpoint.cs","lines":["@@ -6,7 +6,6 @@"," using System.Threading.Tasks;"," using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Razor;"," using Microsoft.CodeAnalysis;","-using Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp.Formatting;"," using Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CodeFixes;"," using Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CodeRefactorings;"," using Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.LanguageServer.Handler;","@@ -50,16 +49,9 @@ internal sealed class CohostCodeActionsResolveEndpoint(","         return resolveParams.TextDocument;","     }"," ","-    protected override Task<CodeAction?> HandleRequestAsync(CodeAction request, TextDocument razorDocument, CancellationToken cancellationToken)","-    {","-        var csharpSyntaxFormattingOptions = razorDocument.GetCSharpSyntaxFormattingOptions(cancellationToken);","-        return HandleRequestAsync(request, razorDocument, csharpSyntaxFormattingOptions, cancellationToken);","-    }","-","-    private async Task<CodeAction?> HandleRequestAsync(","+    protected override async Task<CodeAction?> HandleRequestAsync(","         CodeAction request,","         TextDocument razorDocument,","-        CSharpSyntaxFormattingOptions csh